I am standing on a quiet street.
I am lost.
Suddenly I see a young woman.
She is walking a small dog.
The dog looks like my family's dog, Lola.
I walk over to the woman.
"Excuse me," I say.
"I am looking for the harbour."
The woman stops and listens.
She points back up the street.
"Go straight back to the square," she says.
"And turn right at the museum."
"Thank you very much for the help," I say.
"You are welcome," the woman replies.
I look down at the little dog.
It looks at me.
I walk back toward the square.
Now I know where I am.
